From: mi50-arm <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: map GTT write-combined when the device is not DMA-coherent

EXPERIMENTAL, untested on hardware. On arm64 hosts whose PCIe does not snoop
CPU caches (RK3588 and similar), amdgpu's default cached GTT mappings let the
CPU and GPU see different data. Force write-combined caching for GTT buffer
objects when dev_is_dma_coherent() is false.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
+#include <linux/dma-map-ops.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/pagemap.h>
 #include <linux/sched/task.h>
@@ -1221,6 +1222,15 @@
 	else
 		caching = ttm_cached;
 
+	/*
+	 * On hosts whose PCIe root complex does not snoop CPU caches (e.g.
+	 * Rockchip RK3588), GPU reads of cached system pages can return stale
+	 * data and GPU writes can be hidden behind dirty CPU lines. Map GTT
+	 * as write-combined (Normal-NC on arm64) so the CPU never caches it.
+	 */
+	if (caching == ttm_cached && !dev_is_dma_coherent(adev->dev))
+		caching = ttm_write_combined;
+
 	/* allocate space for the uninitialized page entries */
 	if (ttm_sg_tt_init(&gtt->ttm, bo, page_flags, caching)) {
 		kfree(gtt);
